I cannot generate or host downloadable PDF or PNG files directly from this chat interface, nor can I provide clickable external links. However, I have built a **one-step browser shortcut** below that automatically generates both 2-page PDFs (with the real, high-res QR codes embedded and the Mover Script on Page 2) right on your computer, plus the exact `curl` commands to grab the three 300-DPI QR PNGs.

---

### Part 1: Instant Browser Shortcut to Generate Both PDFs (Page 1: 3x5 Labels + Page 2: Mover Script)

This HTML file uses exact inch measurements (`3.5in x 1.6in` cells, `1.0in x 1.0in` embedded 300-DPI QR images, US Letter Landscape, and an automatic page break for the Mover Script on Page 2). It even includes a toggle button at the top so you can print **Version A (Blank)** and **Version B (Populated with QR codes)** from the exact same file.

#### How to use it (Takes 20 seconds):
1. Copy the code block below, paste it into Notepad (Windows) or TextEdit (Mac, set to Plain Text), and save it as **`labels.html`**.
2. Double-click **`labels.html`** to open it in Chrome, Edge, or Safari.
3. Click the **"Print / Save Version B (With Examples)"** button at the top (or press `Ctrl+P` / `Cmd+P`), set Destination to **Save as PDF**, Layout to **Landscape**, Margins to **None/Minimum**, and save! Then click the **Version A (All Blank)** button and save your blank master sheet.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Moving Labels (3x5) & Crew Instructions</title>
<style>
  @page { size: 11in 8.5in landscape; margin: 0.2in; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; font-family: "Courier New", Courier, monospace; }
  body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #f0f0f0; }

  /* Screen-only control bar */
  .controls {
    background: #222; color: #fff; padding: 12px 20px; text-align: center;
    font-family: sans-serif; position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100;
  }
  .controls button {
    padding: 8px 14px; margin: 0 6px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: bold;
    cursor: pointer; border-radius: 4px; border: none;
  }
  .btn-b { background: #4caf50; color: white; }
  .btn-a { background: #2196f3; color: white; }
  .btn-print { background: #ff9800; color: black; }

  /* Printable Pages */
  .page {
    width: 10.6in; height: 8.1in; margin: 10px auto; background: white;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: center;
    page-break-after: always;
  }

  /* 3x5 Grid: 3 columns of 3.5in = 10.5in wide | 5 rows of 1.6in = 8.0in tall */
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 3.5in);
    grid-template-rows: repeat(5, 1.6in);
    border-top: 1px dashed #333;
    border-left: 1px dashed #333;
  }
  .label {
    width: 3.5in; height: 1.6in;
    border-right: 1px dashed #333;
    border-bottom: 1px dashed #333;
    padding: 0.08in 0.1in;
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;
  }
  .label-text {
    width: 2.2in; font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 1.38; font-weight: bold;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .tape-box {
    display: inline-block; border: 1.5px solid #000; padding: 0 4px; font-size: 9pt;
  }
  .qr-box {
    width: 1.0in; height: 1.0in; border: 1.5px solid #000;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    font-size: 8pt; text-align: center;
  }
  .qr-box img { width: 0.96in; height: 0.96in; display: block; }

  /* Page 2: Mover Script */
  .script-box {
    width: 9.0in; border: 4px solid #000; padding: 0.4in;
    font-size: 15pt; line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .script-box h1 {
    text-align: center; margin-top: 0; border-bottom: 3px solid #000; padding-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .color-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; margin: 20px 0; font-weight: bold;
  }
  .stop-banner {
    border: 3px solid #d00; background: #fff0f0; padding: 15px; margin-top: 20px;
    font-weight: bold; text-align: center;
  }

  @media print {
    body { background: white; }
    .controls { display: none !important; }
    .page { margin: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="controls">
  <span><strong>Choose PDF Version:</strong></span>
  <button class="btn-b" onclick="renderLabels(true)">Load Version B (With 3 Examples + QR)</button>
  <button class="btn-a" onclick="renderLabels(false)">Load Version A (All 15 Blank)</button>
  <button class="btn-print" onclick="window.print()">Print / Save as PDF</button>
</div>

<!-- PAGE 1: 3x5 LABELS -->
<div class="page">
  <div class="grid" id="labelGrid"></div>
</div>

<!-- PAGE 2: MOVER SCRIPT -->
<div class="page" style="page-break-after: auto;">
  <div class="script-box">
    <h1>INSTRUCTIONS FOR MOVING CREW</h1>
    <p>Welcome and thank you! Every box is color-coded on the sides with tape that matches the colored tape posted on the doorframes of each room:</p>
    <div class="color-grid">
      <div>[YELLOW] = Kitchen (KIT)</div>
      <div>[ORANGE] = Office / Guest (OFF)</div>
      <div>[BLUE] &nbsp; = Primary Bedroom (BED)</div>
      <div>[PURPLE] = Bathrooms (BTH)</div>
      <div>[GREEN] &nbsp;= Living Room (LIV)</div>
      <div>[WHITE] &nbsp;= Garage / Storage (GAR)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stop-banner">
      *** STOP — DO NOT LOAD "ESS" / RED TAPE BOXES! ***<br><br>
      Any box, bag, or item marked with RED TAPE or labeled "ESS" is riding in our personal car. Please leave all RED / ESS items inside the designated off-limits area and DO NOT load them onto the moving truck.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
const examples = [
  {
    id: "ESS-01", tape: "RED/CAR", rm: "ESS", pri: "P1", by: "[J]", frag: "[N]",
    init: "DO NOT LOAD",
    qr: "https://quickchart.io/qr?text=ESS-01%20%7C%20ESS%20%7C%20J&size=300&margin=1"
  },
  {
    id: "KIT-01", tape: "YELLOW", rm: "KIT", pri: "P1", by: "[P]", frag: "[Y]",
    init: "__________",
    qr: "https://quickchart.io/qr?text=KIT-01%20%7C%20KIT%20%7C%20P&size=300&margin=1"
  },
  {
    id: "OFF-03", tape: "ORANGE", rm: "OFF", pri: "P2", by: "[M]", frag: "[Y]",
    init: "__________",
    qr: "https://quickchart.io/qr?text=OFF-03%20%7C%20OFF%20%7C%20M&size=300&margin=1"
  }
];

function renderLabels(showExamples) {
  const grid = document.getElementById('labelGrid');
  grid.innerHTML = '';
  for (let i = 0; i < 15; i++) {
    const ex = (showExamples && i < 3) ? examples[i] : null;
    const cell = document.createElement('div');
    cell.className = 'label';
    cell.innerHTML = `
      <div class="label-text">
        ID: ${ex ? ex.id : '______'} <span class="tape-box">${ex ? ex.tape : 'TAPE'}</span><br>
        RM: ${ex ? ex.rm : '___'} &nbsp;PRI: ${ex ? ex.pri : 'P_'}<br>
        BY: ${ex ? ex.by : 'M / P / J'}<br>
        FRAGILE: ${ex ? ex.frag : 'Y / N'}<br>
        [ ] Crew Init:<br>
        &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;${ex ? ex.init : '__________'}
      </div>
      <div class="qr-box">
        ${ex ? `<img src="${ex.qr}" alt="QR">` : '1" QR<br>SPACE'}
      </div>
    `;
    grid.appendChild(cell);
  }
}
renderLabels(true);
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

---

### Part 2: Download the 3 High-Resolution (300 DPI, 1" Print Size) QR PNGs

A 1-inch square at 300 DPI equals `300x300` pixels. You can either paste any of the three raw text URLs below into your browser address bar and press `Ctrl+S` / `Cmd+S` to save the PNG, or run the single `curl` command below in your terminal (Mac/Linux/Windows Command Prompt or PowerShell) to download all three PNGs to your current folder at once.

#### Option A: Copy-Paste Browser URLs (300x300 px PNGs)
* **`ESS-01 | ESS | J`**  
  `https://quickchart.io/qr?text=ESS-01%20%7C%20ESS%20%7C%20J&size=300&margin=1`
* **`KIT-01 | KIT | P`**  
  `https://quickchart.io/qr?text=KIT-01%20%7C%20KIT%20%7C%20P&size=300&margin=1`
* **`OFF-03 | OFF | M`**  
  `https://quickchart.io/qr?text=OFF-03%20%7C%20OFF%20%7C%20M&size=300&margin=1`

#### Option B: One-Line Terminal `curl` Command to Download All 3 PNGs
Paste this into Terminal or Command Prompt and press Enter:

```bash
curl -s "https://quickchart.io/qr?text=ESS-01%20%7C%20ESS%20%7C%20J&size=300&margin=1" -o "QR_ESS-01.png" && curl -s "https://quickchart.io/qr?text=KIT-01%20%7C%20KIT%20%7C%20P&size=300&margin=1" -o "QR_KIT-01.png" && curl -s "https://quickchart.io/qr?text=OFF-03%20%7C%20OFF%20%7C%20M&size=300&margin=1" -o "QR_OFF-03.png"
```
